# Colophon/Capsule Hardware and Setup 🔧

## Current Setup 🖥️

This Geminispace is running on a Debian VPS with a  Gopherspace on port 70 that is running on Gophernicus while gmid is serving up the Geminispace on port 1965.

If I'm on one of my main machines (a Linux box running LCOS and a Windows 11 gaming rig that I also use for retro emulators and VMs) I usually edit the capsule in Geany and upload any changes with Filezilla. 
 
But I prefer to edit it on my phone, where I use a combination of Markor for editing and CX File Explorer using an SFTP connection to sync the changes directly or to upload the changes when I get back to cell signal (there's a lot of places in Wyoming without cell signal). 

## UPDATE: 

With a lot of help from Grok, I now have my GitHub repo set up so that I can edit my capsule from GitHub and it automagically publishes any changes directly and immediately to my capsule. This is nice for several reasons: it provides a singular editor, no need for having the files across multiple systems for edit, and no need to manually sync the changes. I can still fallback to the old manual method if need be.

> I don't plan on having much of an HTTP site, really. Maybe a proxy to serve up the Gemini and Gopher sites for those who won't install Lagrange for some reason. But from now on Geminispace is my home.

